  "goodToKnow": "Inmitten means in the middle of or amid: inmitten der Natur, inmitten von Freunden. It takes the genitive, or von with the dative. It's elevated and literary; in everyday speech, Germans say mitten in: mitten in der Stadt, mitten in der Nacht. From in + Mitte (middle). Similar formal prepositions: inmitten, innerhalb, unweit."
